[{:db/id 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed948579-cdd5-5155-941d-e802c724684f" "question-89d73552-bd61-5afc-9133-1cbf2f95b120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157000 :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(\\pi,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n![](images/50/5018652c7049be48f998af2ceac522f4170475b1e5f5ed6b2daf77d1443eab27.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/9e/9ecc6bbb35ec3b1fc94b49a9da87099480dccbf63447ecd18b812547110b35ef.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/92/92a91186756bb96fcf826be1ac0819b1a1fc7660cbf8ebff300d6e9390f90416.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/4a/4a0d68e1fb2aa93a6e7606cf7c96dcf692d366a0571c36e589810a4276572339.svg)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](images/b9/b93095604beb468dac2fd708fa679379fdcdf273be6ae6a74517ec605e96a88b.svg) \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = e^y\\cos x ,  \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} =e^y\\sin x .\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\pi,0).$ This gives\n\n![](images/16/168592a2f48649e0cd90aa5226a55204435a02477b9f54f09fc22db32327d7b1.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" "question-98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157002 :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/f2/f2e3cce8b785350e4a3d746dfbbb1e805cc490c5a28680a59bb22e266b9c6b48.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/43/43938aea0610386ae1e7cd862b234b326a396a3c06df1cd8d63ba568c9bd5d62.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/81/81b814aff57a058f564080308dd8fbe220994cf0dcbd84b80715ded32c5c96a1.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $\\left(1,0\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157001 :question/problem "Given that \n![](images/43/43ec08d3ac9a00921335912f8e2cf8770397f141b4eebbb4f857fd0be69f7441.svg) \n evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](images/39/398ea92d21b959026a702db0f606915acb31906451a9039925518ca79fa89717.svg)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/5e/5ea286680d2cec429fe920628617d083f47dd53519c2d40f30115dee45a18bc3.svg)\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det \\left( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\right)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](images/14/1488754e319066706880b21fd4642c7b6a75a458770cab254b974b13d35425a2.svg)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](images/c9/c92e0f35c58187af3fe961947e6e96f0cd82cf32bb00cfd4f51ca3c742339e0c.svg) we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\ln y, \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y})=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1) = 0 \\cdot 0 - 1\\cdot 1 = -1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed948579-cdd5-5155-941d-e802c724684f" :question/id #uuid "ed948579-cdd5-5155-941d-e802c724684f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163633" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy+{y}^{2} & {x}^{2}+2xy\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy+{y}^{2} & {x}^{2}+2xy\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy+{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}+2xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+2xy)=2x+2y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2x+2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+2xy)=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x+2y \\\\ 2x+2y & 2x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3dde31b2-4dff-5b09-bd6e-40098b2f0a7a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3dde31b2-4dff-5b09-bd6e-40098b2f0a7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dde31b2-4dff-5b09-bd6e-40098b2f0a7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7bbd3d5c-3ffb-520e-af1f-462296632c8d" "answer-13ee77d7-6a74-593d-8653-f1729b3ea248" "answer-8facc5d4-6498-52b8-8859-3722fd9af6dc" "answer-26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" "answer-20928d65-8941-5d29-b370-bfefac08f5a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bbd3d5c-3ffb-520e-af1f-462296632c8d" :answer/id #uuid "7bbd3d5c-3ffb-520e-af1f-462296632c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13ee77d7-6a74-593d-8653-f1729b3ea248" :answer/id #uuid "13ee77d7-6a74-593d-8653-f1729b3ea248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8facc5d4-6498-52b8-8859-3722fd9af6dc" :answer/id #uuid "8facc5d4-6498-52b8-8859-3722fd9af6dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" :answer/id #uuid "26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20928d65-8941-5d29-b370-bfefac08f5a8" :answer/id #uuid "20928d65-8941-5d29-b370-bfefac08f5a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-89d73552-bd61-5afc-9133-1cbf2f95b120" :question/id #uuid "89d73552-bd61-5afc-9133-1cbf2f95b120" :question/math-academy-id "q-81008" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & -2y\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & -2y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})=2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)=0 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e0ef2dd1-71c9-595b-9973-83cddc9a73a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e0ef2dd1-71c9-595b-9973-83cddc9a73a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ef2dd1-71c9-595b-9973-83cddc9a73a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" :answer-field/choices ["answer-008e34f8-40a2-54bb-a209-4f32b24572dd" "answer-ce81fb39-4c7c-5dd7-83a4-ded095d5a9e6" "answer-c45b8554-38f1-5540-8813-5593409dc832" "answer-47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" "answer-e8fec4ae-162f-5e33-a06a-ab6bd1b856d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-008e34f8-40a2-54bb-a209-4f32b24572dd" :answer/id #uuid "008e34f8-40a2-54bb-a209-4f32b24572dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2x & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce81fb39-4c7c-5dd7-83a4-ded095d5a9e6" :answer/id #uuid "ce81fb39-4c7c-5dd7-83a4-ded095d5a9e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c45b8554-38f1-5540-8813-5593409dc832" :answer/id #uuid "c45b8554-38f1-5540-8813-5593409dc832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" :answer/id #uuid "47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8fec4ae-162f-5e33-a06a-ab6bd1b856d3" :answer/id #uuid "e8fec4ae-162f-5e33-a06a-ab6bd1b856d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" :question/id #uuid "a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102698" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df98d6a0-0de7-5458-a3e0-290cebc7112b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df98d6a0-0de7-5458-a3e0-290cebc7112b" :answer-field/id #uuid "df98d6a0-0de7-5458-a3e0-290cebc7112b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ea12d60-f04d-5899-a453-2a3ac7e6a206" "answer-19ad17a7-e0eb-5580-8a17-cfa45fc556dc" "answer-181ea12e-68f7-5d66-9bfc-073d7aa2c4d3" "answer-395ecdd2-b730-5bb3-87f3-ebb7ee1749ba" "answer-c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ea12d60-f04d-5899-a453-2a3ac7e6a206" :answer/id #uuid "1ea12d60-f04d-5899-a453-2a3ac7e6a206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19ad17a7-e0eb-5580-8a17-cfa45fc556dc" :answer/id #uuid "19ad17a7-e0eb-5580-8a17-cfa45fc556dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-181ea12e-68f7-5d66-9bfc-073d7aa2c4d3" :answer/id #uuid "181ea12e-68f7-5d66-9bfc-073d7aa2c4d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-395ecdd2-b730-5bb3-87f3-ebb7ee1749ba" :answer/id #uuid "395ecdd2-b730-5bb3-87f3-ebb7ee1749ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c" :answer/id #uuid "c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/id #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-102461" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{x}{y}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7" :answer-field/id #uuid "eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-007fcd15-219d-5a7b-979f-5872cbdb9291" "answer-349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" "answer-ea727c2d-0baf-5e14-8734-e9b51371b264" "answer-157d76c9-2e6f-5cdb-897c-847f29e94391" "answer-7529d158-9818-51d1-bf9e-38fc8f2bbd6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-007fcd15-219d-5a7b-979f-5872cbdb9291" :answer/id #uuid "007fcd15-219d-5a7b-979f-5872cbdb9291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/id #uuid "349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea727c2d-0baf-5e14-8734-e9b51371b264" :answer/id #uuid "ea727c2d-0baf-5e14-8734-e9b51371b264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-157d76c9-2e6f-5cdb-897c-847f29e94391" :answer/id #uuid "157d76c9-2e6f-5cdb-897c-847f29e94391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7529d158-9818-51d1-bf9e-38fc8f2bbd6a" :answer/id #uuid "7529d158-9818-51d1-bf9e-38fc8f2bbd6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157792 :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$\nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{3})=2{y}^{3}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{3} & 6x{y}^{2} \\\\ 6x{y}^{2} & 6{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=2\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=-24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186155673 :answer-field/correct 17592186155677 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/id #uuid "f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-102692" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=\\frac{2y}{x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2y}{x} & 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=(-1)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2=-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092" :answer-field/id #uuid "57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" "answer-3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" "answer-4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" "answer-3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" "answer-9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" :answer/id #uuid "e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/id #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" :answer/id #uuid "4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" :answer/id #uuid "3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1" :answer/id #uuid "9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158568 :tutorial/content "We've seen how to calculate the total derivative of a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R.$ In this lesson, we will learn how to calculate its second derivative.\n\nFor a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n\n![](images/44/44a95860d7e7bd926f4d94c2ebb5b037e8537ac622f7c86b500aa06b9f959250.svg)\n\nthe total derivative of $f$ is given by the matrix\n\n![](images/e0/e0c9f72b67a531f992342e9f9e0b74f447de5e2b62c9fd81f08804096a912e67.svg)\n\nTo differentiate $f$ once more, we first need to take the transpose of the first derivative:\n\n![](images/4d/4d23282171c39149eeebd7301550ebdf1727b86736a57de6e5d7b6ea96891157.svg)\n\nTo calculate the **second derivative** of $f,$ we simply apply the definition of the total derivative to $\\left(\\boldsymbol f'(\\mathbf x)\\right)^T.$ By doing this, we get the following $n\\times n$ matrix:\n\n![](images/3d/3d62db0c4018fcce47077285aa05e6c4ea3c79e972ab87fccf5165a07083eda9.svg)\n\nNotice that this matrix is *symmetric* due to the equality of mixed partial derivatives. This becomes important later. \n\nThe matrix $\\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x)$ is sometimes called the **Hessian matrix,** and its determinant, \n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det\\big( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\big)\n$$\n\nis called the **Hessian determinant**.\n\nNote that in the case of a two-variable function $f(x,y),$ the second derivative is given by\n\n![](images/e8/e83195902ce2cdc2e0ff6c1f51ebc679a4bddd51fedd38c4bc6fddc4c73373dd.svg)\n\nIn this lesson, we'll primarily focus on two-variable functions $f(x,y).$ However, we should remember that the techniques discussed here can be applied to scalar functions with an arbitrary number of variables." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157481 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
